  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COME Initiate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COME Initiative aims to build a community that is able to make responsible and informed choices in life by creating a supportive environment by empowering the Youths and Adolescent Girls and Young women (AGYW) to build sustainable, peaceful, tolerant andinclusivecommunity through life skills and ICT development. In Nyalenda slums, Adolescent Girls and Young Women (AGYW) face a lot of challenges with the social and cultural perception that they should only be house wives and take care of children back athome. This has created a situation where there has been an increase in teenage/early marriages and teenage pregnancies which in turn affects their economic competitiveness and advantage. AGYWs living in the local slums of Nyalenda bore the highest bruntofthe COVID 19 Pandemic. There was increased school dropout due to COVID-19 which saw an increased unproductive Adolescent Girls and Young women population who are not taking part in any economic activity leading to increased teenage pregnancies and teenagemarriages as result of socio-cultural pressure. The Jiajiri will empower AGYWs with hands-on skills through vocational trainings on fashion and design (tailoring and dressmaking), making of reusable sanitary towels and entrepreneurship skills while empowering them with information on integrated health issues through creative and participatory life skills sessions.</narrative>
  </description>
